A||||6||Ferrari_cdn||winshield cracked!||||8||
Z||000000||Ferrari_cdn||12-01-2001||01:47 AM||||When I bought the Fiero, it had a really small chip in the windshield, drivers side.  I can't feel it from the inside.  Today after a lot of snowfall, and I went out to drive home from work, I cleaned the snow and scraped it off.  Driving home I found there is a foot and a half long very thin fine crack on the windshield, starting from the chip (both sides).  What do you think I should do, replace the damned thing ASAP with my dad chipping in (bad joke) or do it soon when I can afford it?<P>Cracks get progessively worse overtime in cold weather, right?<P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/ferrari_cdn" TARGET=_blank>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ferrari_cdn.JPG">   </A>  <BR>AIM: CanadianFiero||||reg||8
Z||000001||fropuff||12-01-2001||01:57 AM||||Do you have glass coverage on your insurance policy?||||reg||1
Z||000002||Ferrari_cdn||12-01-2001||02:05 AM||||I dont think so but I'll check.  My brother in law helped me get insurance.  I knew nothing at the time I got my car.||||reg||11
Z||000003||BlackStang95||12-01-2001||02:47 AM||||They get worse over time regardless of weather.  plus you can get pulled over with it.  Get if fixed asap.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Cheever3000||12-01-2001||03:09 AM||||BlackStang's right.  And yours could get worse very soon, or not for a long time, you just never know.  Get it fixed or have a replacement handy.  Search the Forum for how to replace yourself.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||avengador1||12-01-2001||11:11 AM||||As your car's interior heat cycles from cold to hot, the crack will continue to spread. Get it fixed asap.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Avendgador1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Mach10||12-01-2001||04:28 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Ferrari_cdn:<BR><B>I dont think so but I'll check.  My brother in law helped me get insurance.  I knew nothing at the time I got my car.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Yes, you DO have glass coverage. Will cost you your deductible. Wait 'till you can afford it. WPG cops won't pull you over...<P>The crack WILL get worse as the weather gets colder. It'll ONLY be a problem if it starts getting into your viewing area... Otherwise, just wait for a while...<P>Call AutoPAC and claim the glass. They'll tell you just to drag it in, get it fixed, and pay your deductible there.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>||||reg||10
